  "notes": "## Rove 0.1.8 beta\n\n- Delete folders containing subfolders with an explicit confirmation, including their nested requests.\n- Expanded HTTP Body choices: None, JSON, XML, Text, URL-encoded form, Multipart form, Binary, MessagePack and Raw. Improved cURL import classification and exact file/form upload handling.\n- Improved Auth selection and pending credential handling across Request and Case editing.\n- Improved large HTML preview responsiveness and progressive asset handling.\n- Response-aware Code helper for captured variables and aliases, with typed members, JSON field suggestions from saved examples/schema, and guided JSON/header/status actions.\n- Named sequential Script test groups and clearer test results in History, Regression and reports.\n- Documentation code examples for cURL, Fetch and Python, with saved-environment selection and HTML export.\n- Additional fixes for Case ownership, request persistence, draft recovery and execution/report evidence.\n\nWindows x64 and macOS Apple Silicon packages are provided. This is an optional beta update; minimum supported version remains 0.1.1.\n\nRequests saved with the new Body formats require Rove 0.1.8 or newer. Helper suggestions do not execute scripts or send requests; JSON field suggestions describe saved examples/schema rather than guarantee a future response shape. Imported Postman scripts are still reference material and are not automatically executed.\n",
